  "versionHistory": [
    {
      "version": "1.0",
      "releaseNotes": "",
      "seenAt": "2016-07-25T04:02:36Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.1",
      "releaseNotes": "Get ready...\nBecause you can now play Loop&Dot right on your iPhone or iPod!\nSimply swipe up to play.",
      "seenAt": "2016-08-02T02:26:43Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.2",
      "releaseNotes": "Get Set...\nBecause Loop & Dot has a new Settings page accessible with the Gear Icon.\nIn the settings you can change the theme from Light to Dark or turn on the all new Tap mode.  This allows you to tap, rather than swipe, to change Loop's Size.\nAlso, your highest score is displayed right on the Title Page.  No swiping is required when bragging to your friends.",
      "seenAt": "2016-08-11T01:32:02Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.3",
      "releaseNotes": "Go!\nBecause Loop & Dot is now using Game Center!\nThis huge update also allows you to unlock new paint colors as you earn points.\n\nOpen the settings page to paint Loop a new color and the scores page to access Game Center.",
      "seenAt": "2016-08-19T21:45:00Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.4",
      "releaseNotes": "Play an all new Modern Survival mode using power-ups to earn as many points as possible.\n - Use Time to add 10 seconds to the game.\n - Use Double to double your score for 10 seconds.\n - Use lifeline to escape from the enemy once in the game.\n\nHow do you unlock these power-ups?\nNow, when you play either Survival mode, you earn coins for catching Dot.  The higher you score, the more coins you get.\nUse these coins to buy power-ups in the store and bring your scores way up!\nDo not fear, you can still play the original Classic Survival mode from the Levels page.\n\nOn Apple Watch, you now earn coins that you can use to unlock new colors from the Paints page.\nAdditionally, you can now play on your iPad.",
      "seenAt": "2016-09-16T14:55:25Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.5",
      "releaseNotes": "Play an all new Reversed Mode.  \nIn this mode there is no time limit. Instead when the Timer reaches zero, Loop and Dot reverse places.\nIf you do not catch Dot before the Timer reaches zero, you will lose a life.\n\nAlso new:\n- Metallic colors and animations come to Apple Watch.\n- You can now choose \"Play Again\" on Apple Watch.\n- Loop & Dot overall looks better.\n- A new about page allows you to give feedback.\n- The instructions page gets a little more helpful.",
      "seenAt": "2016-12-02T15:00:37Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.5.1",
      "releaseNotes": "Added stickers to iMessage.",
      "seenAt": "2016-12-09T15:01:06Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "1.6",
      "releaseNotes": "Loop & Dot gets an upgrade on Apple Watch!\nA new Tutorials page is available to help get you started and explain how the game pieces work. Access the Tutorials page from the new Levels page. On the Levels page, you will be able to change and control which game mode you are playing as more game modes become available. \n\nAlso new:\n - Added a new color \"Red\" to Apple Watch\n - Added \"Clear Bad Scores\" function on Apple Watch\n - Improved game graphics\n - Better look on Apple Watch\n - Fixed iPad orientation bug",
      "seenAt": "2017-04-15T15:43:02Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.0",
      "releaseNotes": "Happy Thanksgiving!\n\nA major redesign has been in the works for quite some time. Now it is finally here! Some things have changed quite a bit, making for a whole new experience. This means an even better game for you and more new features in the future. \n\nWhat's better in 2.0?\n - Loop & Dot looks great on iPhone X.\n - Added support for iOS 9, 10, and 11.\n - The tutorial page is now the first page you see when you first open the game. No more guessing what to do or where to look.\n - You can now swipe up and down or left and right in the game.\n - There are new complications for Apple Watch, so Loop & Dot can be played even quicker from your wrist.\n - The Classic and Mini game modes are available on both iPhone and Apple Watch.",
      "seenAt": "2017-11-21T15:00:45Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "2.1.1",
      "releaseNotes": "Bug fixes",
      "seenAt": "2018-06-08T14:11:47Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "3.0",
      "releaseNotes": "Completely new. Completely modern.\n\nVersion 3.0 was built from the ground up and brings a long overdue redesign.\nLoop & Dot is all new and now supports the latest Apple Watch models, and versions of WatchOS.",
      "seenAt": "2019-12-31T00:09:59Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "3.0.1",
      "releaseNotes": "- Haptics can be turned off on Apple Watch\n- Share new iMessage Stickers",
      "seenAt": "2020-01-09T12:53:43Z"
    },
    {
      "version": "3.0.2",
      "releaseNotes": "Fixes an issue where Loop & Dot may not launch on Apple Watch.",
      "seenAt": "2020-01-10T14:31:20Z"
    }
  ],
